  "limitations": [
    "Quadratic is a measured-section approximation of the progressive bowl, not an exact Fibonacci/as-built surface. Lane-height RMS residual2\u20132.4cm at core840\u2013900m; original-plane RMS19\u201322cm. Classification/registration uncertainty remains much larger than numeric fit residual.",
    "Source road datum, longitudinal elevations, centreline and full road widths unchanged. The quadratic is anchored at lane0 and preserves that height.",
    "Centreline-to-orthophoto registration allowance approximately 1 m and ground-height allowance 0.5 m are reconstruction estimates. AHN local two-metre slope estimates can reach 19.2 degrees within the marked road. The quadratic matches relative heights more closely than every local derivative; its outer slope can differ by approximately 4.7 degrees at 880 m. Curbs/pixel noise affect edge derivatives. Exact Fibonacci geometry is not claimed.",
    "Transition bank coefficients are interpolated from sparse cross-sections. Near960m only the previously retained2m AHN export is available; neutral quadratic continuation is retained because its small measured inverse crown is below the height allowance.",
    "All other circuits and ZandvoortT14 retain zero quadratic coefficient; vehicle tuning, handling and camera algorithms unchanged."
  ],
